<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73711" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοι-ωτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>assimilative,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>Nat.Fac.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>by means of resemblance, on the basis of analogy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετάβασις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					11.250
				</span></i>
			 : Subst., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span>
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>the art of
			likening</i> or <i>copying,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.126
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					3.40
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> epith. of odd numbers and square numbers (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅμοιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					111.2
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				57
			</span></i>.</div>
